1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,633
The sun blazes overhead.

2
00:00:01,633 --> 00:00:03,833
Cicadas chirp away.

3
00:00:03,833 --> 00:00:05,466
Beelu is drenched in sweat

4
00:00:05,466 --> 00:00:07,900
as he walks along all by himself.

5
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:08,866
Hmph!

6
00:00:08,866 --> 00:00:10,500
Dad is the worst!

7
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:11,900
It's the weekend.

8
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,033
Beelu's family has gone out for a trip,

9
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:15,900
but along the way,

10
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:18,533
Beelu threw a huge tantrum.

11
00:00:18,533 --> 00:00:20,633
As Beelu keeps walking,

12
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:21,800
before he knows it,

13
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:23,733
he arrives at a very lively place.

14
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:25,966
The animals here

15
00:00:25,966 --> 00:00:27,833
some wear little caps

16
00:00:27,833 --> 00:00:29,600
while others wear headscarves.

17
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:32,000
They're chatting and laughing together.

18
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:32,633
Huh?

19
00:00:32,633 --> 00:00:33,700
What's that?

20
00:00:34,233 --> 00:00:37,100
A green archway stands before him.

21
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,100
Atop the archway

22
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:39,700
is a crescent moon.

23
00:00:40,933 --> 00:00:42,000
Behind the archway

24
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,400
is a little green lane.

25
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,167
Inside the lane

26
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:47,000
stands a square-shaped,

27
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,866
large, green building.

28
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,700
What did you say?

29
00:00:53,233 --> 00:00:55,266
A big cat wearing a headscarf

30
00:00:55,266 --> 00:00:57,333
pats Beelu on the shoulder

31
00:00:57,333 --> 00:01:00,403
and speaks in a language he's never heard before.

32
00:01:05,333 --> 00:01:06,433
Sorry,

33
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:08,333
I don't understand.

34
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:10,566
The big cats begin talking among themselves.

35
00:01:10,566 --> 00:01:12,747
A pair of blue-green eyes

36
00:01:12,747 --> 00:01:14,558
stares at Beelu.

37
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:17,575
Their round pupils reflect Beelu's image.

38
00:01:17,575 --> 00:01:20,100
Beelu is frightened.

39
00:01:21,050 --> 00:01:23,466
Before the big cats can speak to him again,

40
00:01:23,466 --> 00:01:25,066
he quickly runs away.

41
00:01:26,966 --> 00:01:28,733
Panting, Beelu

42
00:01:28,733 --> 00:01:30,467
runs into a park.

43
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:32,874
He runs so fast and so hard

44
00:01:32,874 --> 00:01:34,875
that he accidentally...

45
00:01:35,666 --> 00:01:37,766
...runs into an animal!

46
00:01:37,766 --> 00:01:40,100
To his surprise, the one standing in front of him

47
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,900
is another big cat wearing a headscarf.

48
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:44,400
Ah!

49
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,033
The big cat's eyes seem to glow.

50
00:01:47,033 --> 00:01:48,366
He looks so scary!

51
00:01:49,233 --> 00:01:50,333
You...

52
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:52,233
Don't come any closer!

53
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:55,600
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to scare you.

54
00:01:56,133 --> 00:01:57,135
Sit still for a moment.

55
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:59,125
I'll take care of your wound.

56
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:03,100
The big cat moves very gently.

57
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:05,400
His voice is soft and gentle.

58
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:08,333
He slowly walks over to Beelu

59
00:02:08,333 --> 00:02:10,667
and picks up a bandage.

60
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:12,067
My name is Aisha.

61
00:02:12,067 --> 00:02:15,701
There are so many friends here wearing robes and headscarves today

62
00:02:15,701 --> 00:02:18,167
because it's the Eid al-Fitr holiday.

63
00:02:18,967 --> 00:02:20,403
Eid al-Fitr?

64
00:02:21,133 --> 00:02:21,766
That's right.

65
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:25,124
Aisha explains

66
00:02:25,124 --> 00:02:28,889
that Eid al-Fitr is a major Islamic holiday.

67
00:02:28,889 --> 00:02:30,809
During the holiday,

68
00:02:30,809 --> 00:02:32,789
they get together with family

69
00:02:32,789 --> 00:02:34,325
and friends.

70
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:43,966
There, all fixed.

71
00:02:43,966 --> 00:02:45,400
Thank you.

72
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:48,357
It's going to be lively here for the next few days.

73
00:02:48,357 --> 00:02:50,700
If you're not with your mom and dad,

74
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:52,000
it's easy to get lost.

75
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,233
Hmph!

76
00:02:54,233 --> 00:02:55,700
I don't want anything to do with Dad!

77
00:02:56,466 --> 00:02:57,466
Huh?

78
00:02:57,466 --> 00:02:58,433
What's wrong?

79
00:02:59,875 --> 00:03:00,800
It turns out

80
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:03,141
Beelu's mom's birthday is coming up.

81
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:04,924
On this trip,

82
00:03:04,924 --> 00:03:08,700
Beelu wanted to give her a big surprise.

83
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:09,733
I have to find the most delicious cake

84
00:03:09,733 --> 00:03:11,433
for Mom!

85
00:03:12,333 --> 00:03:13,766
The night before,

86
00:03:13,766 --> 00:03:15,433
Beelu and his dad

87
00:03:15,433 --> 00:03:18,120
visited lots of cake shops

88
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:20,400
and finally found

89
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:22,866
the cake they liked best.

90
00:03:23,566 --> 00:03:24,267
But to their surprise,

91
00:03:24,267 --> 00:03:25,767
when they arrived at their destination,

92
00:03:25,767 --> 00:03:27,266
Beelu's dad realized

93
00:03:27,266 --> 00:03:30,133
he'd forgotten to bring the cake.

94
00:03:30,133 --> 00:03:31,400
The surprise Beelu had planned for so long

95
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:34,683
was ruined just like that.

96
00:03:37,667 --> 00:03:40,100
The more Beelu thought about it, the angrier he got.

97
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:42,766
But Aisha didn't reply.

98
00:03:42,766 --> 00:03:45,300
Cicadas chirped in the background.

99
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:46,500
The shadow of a big tree

100
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,633
swayed gently in the breeze.

101
00:03:50,403 --> 00:03:51,700
Beelu,

102
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:53,033
actually,

103
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:54,933
I'm a little envious of you.

104
00:03:54,933 --> 00:03:56,833
Huh? Envious?

105
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:58,866
Why?

106
00:03:58,866 --> 00:04:00,333
Well...

107
00:04:00,333 --> 00:04:01,766
How should I put it?

108
00:04:05,267 --> 00:04:06,666
Are you hungry?

109
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:09,066
Yeah.

110
00:04:09,066 --> 00:04:12,133
After Beelu got separated from his parents,

111
00:04:12,133 --> 00:04:13,400
he hadn't eaten anything.

112
00:04:14,333 --> 00:04:15,566
Here's what we'll do.

113
00:04:15,566 --> 00:04:17,435
There's a lively event up ahead,

114
00:04:17,435 --> 00:04:19,291
and lots of delicious food there.

115
00:04:19,291 --> 00:04:21,566
Let's talk while we walk.

116
00:04:23,267 --> 00:04:26,250
They arrive at a lively place.

117
00:04:26,250 --> 00:04:28,200
Unfamiliar

118
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:30,544
yet lively voices fill their ears.

119
00:04:30,544 --> 00:04:33,450
The stalls are lined with all kinds

120
00:04:33,450 --> 00:04:35,400
of colorful foods Beelu has never seen before.

121
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,775
The signs

122
00:04:36,775 --> 00:04:39,233
are decorated with unusual pictures and writing.

123
00:04:40,980 --> 00:04:41,980
Look!

124
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:43,467
This is called Nyonya kuih.

125
00:04:43,467 --> 00:04:45,233
I made all of these!

126
00:04:45,933 --> 00:04:48,280
On a large porcelain plate

127
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,666
sit rows of little square cakes,

128
00:04:49,666 --> 00:04:52,566
giving off a sweet, delicious aroma.

129
00:04:53,366 --> 00:04:54,325
Wow!

130
00:04:54,325 --> 00:04:57,167
They look so tasty!

131
00:04:57,167 --> 00:04:58,667
They're made to celebrate the holiday

132
00:04:58,667 --> 00:05:00,683
and welcome visitors.

133
00:05:00,683 --> 00:05:02,800
It's my favorite dessert.

134
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,033
You're amazing!

135
00:05:06,410 --> 00:05:07,871
When I was little, during holidays and New Year,

136
00:05:07,871 --> 00:05:11,091
I always looked forward to eating the Nyonya kuih my mom made.

137
00:05:11,091 --> 00:05:13,011
But after I grew up and started working,

138
00:05:13,011 --> 00:05:14,750
Mom wasn't around anymore,

139
00:05:14,750 --> 00:05:17,049
so I had to learn to make them myself.

140
00:05:20,133 --> 00:05:22,566
Where is your mom?

141
00:05:22,566 --> 00:05:25,200
My family doesn't live here.

142
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:28,233
I haven't seen them in three years.

143
00:05:28,233 --> 00:05:30,467
What? Three years!

144
00:05:30,467 --> 00:05:33,902
Aisha says three years isn't that long.

145
00:05:33,902 --> 00:05:36,252
Many friends here are just like her.

146
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:38,150
They come from other countries

147
00:05:38,150 --> 00:05:40,600
to work far away from home.

148
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:43,279
They stay for several years at a time.

149
00:05:43,279 --> 00:05:45,979
They can't even go home for the holidays.

150
00:05:49,366 --> 00:05:52,300
Don't you miss them?

151
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:53,554
Of course I do.

152
00:05:53,554 --> 00:05:57,550
I've finally learned to make delicious Nyonya kuih,

153
00:05:57,550 --> 00:05:59,067
but sadly, my parents

154
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:01,333
are on the other end of the phone

155
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:02,333
and can't taste them.

156
00:06:03,566 --> 00:06:05,133
Oh...

157
00:06:05,133 --> 00:06:06,833
So, Beelu,

158
00:06:06,833 --> 00:06:08,700
I'm a little envious of you.

159
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:12,375
Even though your mom can't taste the cake you prepared,

160
00:06:12,375 --> 00:06:16,325
your whole family can still be together.

161
00:06:18,225 --> 00:06:20,699
Hearing Aisha's words,

162
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:25,435
Suddenly, Beelu longs to find his parents.

163
00:06:29,775 --> 00:06:33,333
Could you help me make a phone call?

164
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:36,300
Mom and Dad must be worried about me now.

165
00:06:36,300 --> 00:06:37,266
Of course.

166
00:06:37,266 --> 00:06:37,700
Ah!

167
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:41,633
But I threw such a big tantrum this morning.

168
00:06:41,633 --> 00:06:42,533
Do you think Mom and Dad

169
00:06:42,533 --> 00:06:45,300
might be mad at me, too?

170
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:46,466
Hmm...

171
00:06:46,466 --> 00:06:48,100
I have an idea.

172
00:06:52,033 --> 00:06:55,433
Hello? Is our Beelu there?

173
00:06:57,133 --> 00:06:58,233
As soon as they get the call,

174
00:06:58,233 --> 00:06:59,933
Beelu's mom and dad

175
00:06:59,933 --> 00:07:01,433
hurry over.

176
00:07:02,533 --> 00:07:04,075
He's over there!

177
00:07:05,666 --> 00:07:07,800
All the vendors have packed up.

178
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:11,033
Only Aisha and Beelu are still busy.

179
00:07:11,666 --> 00:07:14,713
He said he wanted to make the most delicious Nyonya kuih

180
00:07:14,713 --> 00:07:17,467
for you to eat.

181
00:07:17,467 --> 00:07:18,967
Beelu...

182
00:07:18,967 --> 00:07:21,466
Dad is so sorry.

183
00:07:22,333 --> 00:07:24,403
Dad! Mom!

184
00:07:25,733 --> 00:07:28,300
The moon hangs high in the sky.

185
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:31,331
Laughter fills the house.

186
00:07:32,775 --> 00:07:36,850
Beelu's family and their new friends gather together

187
00:07:36,850 --> 00:07:41,333
and share a delicious meal from another culture, making it an unforgettable evening.

188
00:07:42,667 --> 00:07:43,667
The big cats

189
00:07:43,667 --> 00:07:45,500
speak an unfamiliar language

190
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:47,779
and wear unusual clothes.

191
00:07:47,779 --> 00:07:51,108
They also have big, round blue eyes.

192
00:07:51,108 --> 00:07:55,396
But Beelu is no longer afraid of them.

193
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,266
Today was so much fun!
